AFRICAN UNION
CULTURAL LINGUISTIC INTEGRATION CERTIFICATE

This certifies that the Republic of Zambia, through its legislative and civic processes, has formally inducted Bemba and Lozi as official national languages, affirming their cultural, legal, and administrative status in alignment with AU Agenda 2063 and ACALAN protocols.

This certificate acknowledges:
✓ Cultural sovereignty of Zambian linguistic heritage
✓ AU-aligned language revitalization milestones
✓ Continental support for multilingual governance

Issued this day, June 2025.

Signed:
Chairperson, AU Commission for Culture and Heritage
Endorsed:
UNESCO Liaison Officer – Southern Africa
